---
title: "Audit Logging"
description: "Configure structured JSON audit logging for the QQL gateway — request logging, denied request tracking, and log format."
sidebar:
  order: 7
---

The gateway writes a structured JSON line for every request. Use it for compliance, debugging, and security analysis.

## Enable

{% terminal title="Enable audit logging" %}
qql-go serve \
  --audit \
  --audit-file audit.jsonl   # omit to write to stderr
{% /terminal %}

## Log Format

Each request produces one JSON line:

**Successful request:**

```json
{
  "ts": "2026-06-18T10:00:00Z",
  "subject": "usr_alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "tenant_id": "acme-corp",
  "roles": ["reader"],
  "operation": "EXEC",
  "collection": "docs",
  "query": "QUERY 'company' FROM docs LIMIT 5",
  "status": "ok",
  "latency_ms": 12,
  "allowed": true
}
```

**Denied request:**

```json
{
  "ts": "2026-06-18T10:00:01Z",
  "subject": "usr_bob",
  "operation": "EXEC",
  "status": "denied",
  "denied": "true",
  "denied_reason": "operation DELETE not permitted for current token",
  "latency_ms": 1
}
```

## Fields

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| `ts` | ISO 8601 timestamp |
| `subject` | JWT `sub` claim |
| `email` | JWT `email` claim (if present) |
| `tenant_id` | Extracted tenant claim |
| `roles` | Extracted role claim(s) |
| `operation` | RPC type (`EXEC`, `EXEC_BATCH`, `EXPLAIN`, `HEALTH`, `CONVERT`) |
| `collection` | Target collection name |
| `query` | The QQL query string (as received) |
| `status` | `ok` or `denied` |
| `latency_ms` | End-to-end request latency in milliseconds |
| `allowed` | `true` if the request passed policy |
| `denied` | `"true"` if the request was denied |
| `denied_reason` | Human-readable denial reason |

## Implementation

Audit logging uses a context-passing pattern:

1. The interceptor creates an empty `AuditMeta` in the request context.
2. The handler fills it with AST details (collection name, operation type, query text).
3. After execution, the interceptor builds the final JSON entry and writes it.

{% aside type="note" title="Original Query Captured" %}
This ensures the audit log captures the **original query** (before AST injection), not the rewritten one.
{% /aside %}

## Querying Audit Logs

Since each line is JSON, you can query with `jq`:

{% terminal title="Query audit logs with jq" %}
# All denied requests
jq 'select(.status == "denied")' audit.jsonl

# Requests by tenant
jq 'select(.tenant_id == "acme-corp")' audit.jsonl

# Slow queries (> 100ms)
jq 'select(.latency_ms > 100)' audit.jsonl

# All DROP operations
jq 'select(.query | startswith("DROP"))' audit.jsonl
{% /terminal %}
